-- title:
--   Fibrewise flatness yields flat stalk quotients
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $f \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a smooth separated morphism of schemes, and let $h \colon X \to X$ satisfy $f \circ h = f$ (in diagrammatic form, $h$ followed by $f$ equals $f$). Fix a point $x$ of $X$ and assume that for every point $s$ of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ the endomorphism `schemeFibreEndo f h hcomm s` of the pullback of $f$ along the canonical morphism $\operatorname{Spec} \kappa(s) \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ — namely the morphism induced by the first projection followed by $h$ together with the second projection — is a flat morphism of schemes. Write $y = h(x)$ and $z = f(h(x))$. The stalk maps $\mathcal{O}_{\operatorname{Spec} R, z} \to \mathcal{O}_{X,y}$ induced by $f$ and $\mathcal{O}_{X,y} \to \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ induced by $h$, together with their composite, make the three stalks a tower of algebras. Let $\mathfrak{m} \subseteq \mathcal{O}_{\operatorname{Spec} R, z}$ be the maximal ideal. The conclusion is that $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}/\mathfrak{m}^{e}$, where $\mathfrak{m}^{e}$ denotes the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}$ under the composite stalk map, is a flat module over $\mathcal{O}_{X,y}/\mathfrak{m}\mathcal{O}_{X,y}$, the algebra structure being the one induced on quotients from the inclusion of the images of $\mathfrak{m}$.
--
--   This is the stalk-level translation of fibrewise flatness: it converts flatness of the induced endomorphisms of all the fibres of $f$ into flatness of the corresponding map of fibre rings at a point, the form in which the local criterion of flatness is applied. It is used in the treatment of the relative group law on a Jacobian with good reduction, to prove flatness of multiplication by $n$ from its flatness on fibres, and it rests on the identification of the kernel of the stalk map of the fibre inclusion with the extension of the maximal ideal of the base stalk ([`AlgebraicGeometry.ker_fiberIota_stalkMap_eq_maximalIdeal_map`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ker_fiberIota_stalkMap_eq_maximalIdeal_map)).
